        "rationale": "`_handle_stop` now calls `capturar_lancamentos` on every Stop, before checking `verified`. While a launch is `pendente`, `notificacoes_de` opens and scans the whole transcript line by line; the substring filter skips the JSON parse but not the read. On main, Stop cost nothing extra here. During a ~21 min suite, every intermediate Stop pays for reading a transcript that can run to tens of MB. If the transcript disappears (OSError -> `continue`) or the notification never matches, the launch never leaves `pendente` and keeps getting re-read on every Stop and every `complete`. There is no attempt limit and no TTL. It only degrades latency, not correctness.",
